An issue within the `zassert_equal` macro on some versions of Zephyr causes it to fail when a negative literal is used as the second argument. The fix is to swap the arguments, placing the negative literal `-EINVAL` as the first argument to the macro. This works around the preprocessor issue without changing the logic of the test.

